Description: Google Sans Flex and Google Sans typefaces
 Google Sans Flex is the variable typeface of Android and Googlebook, with
 weight, width, optical size, slant and roundness axes. Kernora uses it for
 the shell, its apps, window titles and KDE and GTK apps.
 .
 Google Sans Flex has no Cyrillic, Greek or most non-Latin scripts, so the
 package also ships Google Sans and a fontconfig rule that takes those
 letters from Google Sans.
